<title>USA: Four Tampa Electric workers hurt in mishap.</title>
<headline>Four Tampa Electric workers hurt in mishap.</headline>
<dateline>TAMPA, Fla. 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Four workers at Tampa Electric Co, a unit of TECO Energy Inc, were injured Thursday in an accident at a power plant, a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>The four men were injured when slag produced by coal used to power the plant overflowed. Two of the men suffered burns, but the injuries to all four were described by the spokesman as not severe.</p>
<p>The workers were taken to Tampa General Hospital and were expected to be released later Thursday, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>The plant was taken off line and was exected to be back in service late Thursay or Friday.</p>
<p>((--Miami Bureau, 305-374-5013))</p>
